    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0120" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.022/10–2951</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lovett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-29">29 October
                        1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I refer to the letter of
                    August 27, 1951, by the Deputy Under Secretary of State,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d20-f1"/> in which he requested a study of the strategic value of
                    certain islands in the Pacific claimed by the United States which are also
                    claimed by Great Britain or New Zealand.</p>
                <p>There is inclosed a memorandum to the Secretary of Defense by the Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff which sets forth their evaluation of these islands from a strategic point
                    of view.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>For the Secretary of Defense:</item>
                            <item>K. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kreps</hi>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel, USAF, Deputy Director Executive
                                    Office of the Secretary</hi>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d20-a1.xml" xpointer="d20-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
